{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1277, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given two positive integers N and M.\nLet X = \\displaystyle\\sum_{i = 0}^{M} N^i. If X \\leq 10^9, print the value of X. If X > 10^9, print inf.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN M\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the value of X or inf as specified by the problem statement.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1 \\leq N \\leq 10^9\n- 1 \\leq M \\leq 100\n- All input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n7 3\n\nSample Output 1\n\n400\r\n\nX = 1 + 7 + 49 + 343 = 400. Since 400 \\leq 10^9, print 400.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n1000000 2\n\nSample Output 2\n\ninf\r\n\nX = 1000001000001 > 10^9, so print inf.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n999999999 1\n\nSample Output 3\n\n1000000000\n\nSample Input 4\n\n998244353 99\n\nSample Output 4\n\ninf\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1311, "char_start": 1289, "quote": "Input:\n7 3\nOutput:\n400", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1351, "char_start": 1323, "quote": "Input:\n1000000 2\nOutput:\ninf", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 1400, "char_start": 1363, "quote": "Input:\n999999999 1\nOutput:\n1000000000", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R6", "source": {"char_end": 1443, "char_start": 1412, "quote": "Input:\n998244353 99\nOutput:\ninf", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 4: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "bf440af60bdfe9939534a0f1144892ed6be1b629313cadedc4a9878170d34130", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "a28b88dd6b8598c7d6ca1e02a0ab0a6408e39d38ebebfb66de477b6fbf633899", "seq": 2}
